From 4550000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: wcn36xx: fix NULL deref in the RX survey path

The survey update on every received frame dereferences
wcn->hw->wiphy->bands[band] without a NULL check.  On a 2GHz-only part
(rf_id == RF_IRIS_WCN3620) the 5GHz band is never registered, and
wcn36xx_rx_skb() feeds it hw->conf.chandef.chan->band unchecked.  During a
vif/phy teardown (AP+STA channel sync, service restart, wcn36xx stop) that
channel pointer is stale or zeroed, so band reads as a value with no
registered band and bands[band] is NULL -- sband->channels then panics the
kernel from IRQ context.

Observed on HMUF02-V5: Oops at wcn36xx_rx_skb+0x168 (inlined
wcn36xx_update_survey) right after a vif-delete storm while testing station
mode, kernel panic, device reboot.

The survey is best-effort telemetry (iw survey); skip the update when the
band is not registered.

---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/wcn36xx/txrx.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/wcn36xx/txrx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/wcn36xx/txrx.c
@@ -286,6 +286,9 @@ static void wcn36xx_update_survey(struct wcn36xx *wcn, int rssi, int snr,
 		idx = wcn->hw->wiphy->bands[NL80211_BAND_2GHZ]->n_channels;
 
 	sband = wcn->hw->wiphy->bands[band];
+	if (!sband)
+		return;
+
 	channel = sband->channels;
 
 	for (i = 0; i < sband->n_channels; i++, channel++) {
